WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:03.159
Archer burst onto the scene in 2009,

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:03.720
"HEY!

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.240
PHRASING!"

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:08.260
winning a loyal FX audience and rave reviews
from critics.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:13.610
Adam Reed's spy spoof mixed James Bond with
The Simpsons and the quick-fire bite of Arrested

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.610
Development.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.900
With the time-hopping eighth season going
full-on film noir, it's a perfect time to

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.780
head into the Danger Zone ...

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.500
"DANGER ZONE!"

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.820
… and reveal some facts you may not have
known about Archer.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.789
The Ghost Behind the Spy

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:34.860
Way back in 1994, Cartoon Network took a chance
on an insane idea: a cartoon talk show hosted

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.090
by a throw-away superhero from the 1960s.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.930
That's what gave birth to Space Ghost Coast
to Coast.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:45.070
That was the show that eventually spawned
the insanity of the Adult Swim programming

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.610
block, which has since become a cultural force
on television.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.980
But it also led to the insanity of Archer
many years later...

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:57.100
"This is about conducting espionage operations
for years without any authority or permission

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.600
whatsoever from the U.S. government."

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.580
"Wait — what?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.120
Mother!"

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.940
Archer showrunner Adam Reed got his start
working on Space Ghost as a writer during

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.590
seasons four through six.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.920
Reed then got to make his own show: Sealab
2021, a parody straight out of the Space Ghost

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.780
school of spoofing Hanna-Barbera cartoons.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.789
The original 1972 show was Sealab 2020, an
animated series set in the then-distant future,

00:01:21.789 --> 00:01:27.600
where scientists lived under the sea and … that's
all anyone remembers, because the show lasted

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.079
less than three months.

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:34.630
Reed's parody had a longer life, and for good
reason: it was hilarious … and very Archer:

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.929
"Who needs X-Ray vision?

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:41.329
They'll beg to show their BLEEP to my robot."

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:46.969
All that spoofing of '60s and '70s cartoons
sharpened Reed's comic voice, leading to Archer,

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:49.219
and thus, a legend was born …

00:01:49.219 --> 00:01:51.490
Let's Be Real

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:56.689
Reed and executive producer Matt Thompson
used the real-life faces of friends, acquaintances,

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:01.179
and industry pros from their home base of
Atlanta to create the look of many Archer

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:02.179
characters.

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:07.250
As Vulture reported in 2013, Malory Archer
is based on Atlanta actress — and Jessica

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.970
Walter doppelganger — Kathleen Cohen …

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.800
Sterling Archer comes from model Jason Fitzgerald
...

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.470
Atlanta antiques dealer Candi McElhannon is
the face of Pam …

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.380
And Kynyetta Lester — a Hooters waitress
Reed met after a monster truck rally — serves

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.730
as the model for Lana.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:27.860
While Chris Parnell looks a lot like the character
he voices, Cyril, he's actually not the model.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:33.250
Instead, the animators turned to Atlanta restaurateur
Stuart Fierman for inspiration.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.750
Then there's Lucky Yates.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.720
He voices Krieger, but he's actually the facial
inspiration for Ray, who's in turn played

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.830
by show creator Adam Reed.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:42.830
Confusing enough?

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.150
"What are we thinking?

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.150
What are we doing?"

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.150
"What are we wearing?"

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.580
"My crisis vest, Mr. Fatface."

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.290
As for Krieger, his face belongs to Ben Brieger,
Reed's former college classmate, which is

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.900
how Krieger got his name.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.400
Brieger volunteered his real name, but Reed
altered it slightly, to give the man some

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.400
dignity ...

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.060
"Well, at least you got some closure."

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.840
"Which is more than I ever got."

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.850
"Oh, you are just your mother all over!"

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.650
Lucky's Early Years

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:15.300
Speaking of Lucky Yates, the voice behind
Archer's mad scientist, Krieger, his first

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.150
high-profile acting gig was on … The Food
Network?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.150
It's true.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.690
Yates played a wide variety of characters
on Alton Brown's wacky cooking show Good Eats,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.510
including a fishmonger, a butcher, and the
infamous dungeon master …

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:34.520
"You've been a very bad dungeon master, and
as punishment, I want you to go skim the moat."

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.460
"OHH!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.460
Haha!

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:37.920
Lucky straw!"

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.990
In a Reddit "Ask Me Anything," Yates had nothing
but praise for Brown, saying the famous foodie

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.870
is even more hilarious in real life.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.730
Crossing the Line

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.000
Archer is undeniably edgy.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.160
It's violent, sexually explicit, and unafraid
to poke fun at, well, just about everything

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.220
"Nice job, Oliver Cromwell."

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.330
"I killed a pope!"

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.890
But believe it or not, some scenarios are
forbidden even on Archer.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:06.830
According to showrunner Adam Reed, one script
had Archer disarming a terrorist by throwing

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.950
his baby boy, Seamus, at him.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.240
This didn't sit well with the folks at FX,
who told Reed:

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.600
"We're not a network that throws babies!"

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.120
A bold stance.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.549
It wasn't the only time FX put up a fight.

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:23.060
In season two, a young German girl hits on
Archer, and in the original script, she was

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.219
only 14.

00:04:24.219 --> 00:04:26.810
FX said that was not okay.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:30.370
Eventually, the two sides came to an agreement,
settling for 16.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.849
Amazingly, the age actually issue made it
into the show:

00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:38.340
"I am from Germany … where the age of consent
is 14."

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.720
"What is it, the Alabama of Europe?"

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.520
"In many ways, yes."

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.430
Archer Imitating Life

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:49.409
In season four, Malory Archer married a car
dealership owner named Ron Cadillac, much

00:04:49.409 --> 00:04:51.479
to the chagrin of Sterling Archer.

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:56.439
Cadillac is voiced by Ron Liebman, who is
not only Rachel's awful dad on Friends ...

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.920
"Why would you bring me sewage?"

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.660
… but is also actually married to Jessica
Walter, who voices Malory.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.760
The thespian couple has been hitched since
1983 and were both known more for their dramatic

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.580
work until late into their careers ...

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.259
"I don't know how to wrassle."

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:15.840
"That's alright.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:16.840
She'll show you."

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.360
"Alright, boss."

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.900
Malory Archer would never stand for that ...

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.610
Krieger's Codes

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.110
When it comes to hidden jokes and messages,
Archer is nearly unmatched.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:33.039
Take, for example, the elaborate easter egg
leading fans to Krieger's secret website.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:37.289
It's complicated, but here's the gist: In
season six, there's a brief shot of serial

00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:40.169
number associated with the character Conway
Stern.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:44.409
If you plug that number into something called
a hex code translator, you get the address

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:45.879
for a YouTube video.

00:05:45.879 --> 00:05:49.999
From there, you have to fall far down the
rabbit hole to get the Krieger's site, including

00:05:49.999 --> 00:05:54.840
translating the sound in the YouTube clip
into an additional code, then using that code

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.090
to make your way to a fake Craigslist ad,
crack some more codes … and on and on.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:05.379
Once you arrive, the username and password
is, hilariously, "Krieger" and "guest."

00:06:05.379 --> 00:06:10.020
Once you're logged in, you can play games,
view images, and download Krieger's actual

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.650
in-show ringtone, "Teutonic Butts" ...

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.889
"I tried Cyril, Pam, Cheryl, now I'm even
trying Krieger!"

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:17.480
"Where the hell is everybody?"

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.880
"Teutonic butts teutonic butts …"

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:25.520
It's a fitting, thoroughly bonkers tribute
to a thoroughly bonkers character.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.520
"Smokebomb!"

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.819
Thanks for watching!

00:06:27.819 --> 00:06:30.819
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:30.819 --> 00:06:33.169
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

